      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "0806.2366_p1_b7",
      "text": "In Combinatorics Stirling numbers may be de\ufb01ned in several way. One such\nde\ufb01nition is given in [1], where an extensive consideration of Stirling numbers\nis presented.\n",
      "bbox": [
        133.8,
        258.81,
        477.57,
        292.65
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        535,
        1035,
        1910,
        1170
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 166,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "0806.2366_p1_b8",
      "text": "In this paper an alternative de\ufb01nition of Stirling numbers of both kind is\ngiven. Namely, Stirling numbers of the \ufb01rst kind appear in the closed formula\nfor the n-th derivative of f(ln x).\nIn the same way Stirling numbers of the\nsecond kind appear in the formula for the n-th derivative of f(ex). Here f(x) is\nan arbitrary smooth real function.\n",
      "bbox": [
        133.8,
        294.69,
        477.54,
        352.41
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        535,
        1178,
        1910,
        1409
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 344,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "0806.2366_p1_b9",
      "text": "This facts allow us to de\ufb01ne Stirling numbers within the frame of di\ufb00eren-\ntial calculus. These de\ufb01nitions may be interesting because arbitrary functions\nappear in them. Choosing suitable function we may obtain di\ufb00erent properties\nof Stirling numbers by the use of derivatives only.\n",
      "bbox": [
        133.8,
        354.45,
        477.56,
        400.29
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        535,
        1417,
        1910,
        1601
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 282,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "0806.2366_p1_b10",
      "text": "Using simple properties of derivatives we obtain here three important prop-\nerties of Stirling numbers. First are so called two terms recurrence relations,\nfrom which one can easily derive the combinatorial meaning of Stirling numbers.\n",
      "bbox": [
        133.8,
        402.21,
        477.6,
        436.17
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        535,
        1608,
        1910,
        1744
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 235,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "0806.2366_p1_b11",
      "text": "Next we obtain expansion formulas of powers into falling factorials, and vise\nversa. These expansions usually serve as the de\ufb01nitions of Stirling numbers, as\nin [1].\n",
      "bbox": [
        133.8,
        438.09,
        477.57,
        472.05
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        535,
        1752,
        1910,
        1888
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 165,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "0806.2366_p1_b12",
      "text": "Finally, we obtain the exponential generating functions for Stirling and Bell\nnumbers.\n",
      "bbox": [
        133.8,
        473.97,
        477.48,
        495.93
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        535,
        1895,
        1909,
        1983
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 86,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "0806.2366_p1_b13",
      "text": "As a by product the closed formulas for the n-th derivative of the functions\nf(ex) and f(ln x) are obtained.\n",
      "bbox": [
        133.8,
        497.6,
        477.45,
        519.81
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        535,
        1990,
        1909,
        2079
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "CMR10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 108,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "0806.2366_p1_b14",
      "text": "Stirling numbers of the \ufb01rst kind\n",
